      "quote": "Search key terms were \"Socioeconomic status\", \"nutrition\", \"middle and low income countries\", language, having an abstract and describing factors contributing towards overweight and obesity... 2(7.5%) restricted to adolescents... 10(37%) did not include body mass index (BMI) as an outcome... One (3.7%) study was further excluded restricted to obesity in males.",
      "reason": "Some population/outcome criteria (women, BMI, adults, relevance to overweight/obesity) can be inferred from exclusion reasons, but eligible study designs, settings, and explicit framework-based inclusion criteria are not systematically specified."
